---
import PlatformLogo from '../components/PlatformLogo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"Download Blanc Browser for macOS, Windows, and Linux"}
  description={"Download the free Blanc desktop browser for macOS, Windows, or Linux. Built-in ad and tracker blocking, private tabs, and a minimal island interface."}
  path="/download"
  page="download"
  current="download"
  ogDescription={"A minimal desktop browser with built-in ad and tracker blocking, private tabs, and a floating island interface."}
>
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Download", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/download" }
  ]
}
</script>

<main id="main-content" class="download-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb breadcrumb--page" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">download</span></nav>
  <section class="download-hero" aria-labelledby="download-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">get blanc</p>
    <h1 id="download-title">Download Blanc for macOS, Windows, or Linux.</h1>
    <p>Choose your desktop. Free browser. Patron adds saved Named Workspaces.</p>
  </section>

  <aside class="download-handheld" data-handheld-note hidden aria-labelledby="handheld-title">
    <h2 id="handheld-title">On a phone or tablet?</h2>
    <p>Blanc is a desktop browser for macOS, Windows and Linux.</p>
    <a class="download-handheld-action" href="/download" data-handheld-share="download-share-status" data-handheld-label="Send to my computer" data-handheld-text="Blanc is a desktop browser for macOS, Windows and Linux.">Send to my computer</a>
    <p id="download-share-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </aside>

  <section class="download-options" id="download-options" data-download-options aria-label="Choose a Blanc download">
    <a class="platform-card" id="dl-mac-arm64" data-download-link data-platform="mac-arm64" data-track="download_click" data-cta-position="platform-card" href="/dl/mac-arm64">
      <span class="platform-label platform-label--macos"><PlatformLogo platform="apple" />macOS</span>
      <strong>Mac — Apple Silicon</strong>
      <span>arm64 DMG · signed and notarized</span>
    </a>
    <a class="platform-card" id="dl-mac-x64" data-download-link data-platform="mac-x64" data-track="download_click" data-cta-position="platform-card" href="/dl/mac-x64" hidden>
      <span class="platform-label platform-label--macos"><PlatformLogo platform="apple" />macOS</span>
      <strong>Mac — Intel</strong>
      <span>x64 DMG · signed and notarized</span>
    </a>
    <a class="platform-card" id="dl-win" data-download-link data-platform="win" data-track="download_click" data-cta-position="platform-card" href="/dl/win">
      <span class="platform-label"><PlatformLogo platform="windows" />Windows</span>
      <strong>Download for Windows</strong>
      <span>signed NSIS installer</span>
    </a>
    <a class="platform-card" id="dl-linux" data-download-link data-platform="linux" data-track="download_click" data-cta-position="platform-card" href="/dl/linux">
      <span class="platform-label"><PlatformLogo platform="linux" />Linux</span>
      <strong>Download for Linux</strong>
      <span>AppImage · signed checksum manifest</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <p class="download-whatsnew"><a href="/changelog" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="changelog" data-cta-position="download-options">See what changed in the latest release</a></p>

  <section class="download-details fit-block" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">before you choose</p><h2 id="fit-title">Is Blanc a good fit?</h2></div>
    <div class="download-detail-list">
      <article><h3>A compact everyday workflow</h3><p>Open your inbox and a few articles. Preview a tab’s dot, select it, then use the full list or Cmd/Ctrl+L to find an article by name. Save a Favorite, group related tabs, and use built-in blocking while you browse.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Check the integrations you rely on</h3><p>Blanc has no general third-party extension runtime. Its optional, user-invoked 1Password bridge and device-bound Touch ID passkeys are macOS-only. Synced provider passkeys, including iCloud Keychain, are not supported. If your workflow depends on an extension, check that limitation before switching.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Free essentials; optional saved sets</h3><p>Browsing essentials and ordinary tab groups are free. Blanc Patron is the optional subscription: US$30 per year or US$4 per month, plus applicable tax. It adds saved Named Workspaces. Creating a named workspace requires an active Patron subscription.</p><p>If membership lapses, existing workspaces remain openable, switchable, and automatically updated. Renaming and removing existing workspaces continue to work if it lapses. Earlier one-time supporters keep their lifetime Patron access.</p><a class="text-link" href="/support#workspaces">How Named Workspaces work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="download-details" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">before you install</p>
      <h2 id="trust-title">What you're actually downloading.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="download-detail-list">
      <article>
        <h3>macOS, signed and notarized</h3>
        <p>Every macOS build is code-signed and notarized with Apple, so Gatekeeper verifies it before first launch. This applies to the macOS builds specifically.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Updates arrive in place</h3>
        <p>Installed release builds check GitHub Releases and update themselves automatically — no separate updater, no account.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Bounded usage counts, with an off switch</h3>
        <p>On a fresh profile usage measurement is presented on, but nothing sends until you save the choice and you can turn it off before continuing. When enabled, Blanc counts launches, the first real Mahjong move, and which fixed start-page layouts render—never browsing history, URLs, searches, page content, game state, or private-tab feature activity. <a href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="truth-note download-note" aria-labelledby="windows-note-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">a note for windows</p>
    <h2 id="windows-note-title">Check the publisher, not just the filename.</h2>
    <p>Public Windows releases are Authenticode-signed and the release pipeline refuses an unsigned installer. Windows should report the publisher named on the official release. Stop if the signature is absent, invalid, or names someone else. Download only here or from the <a href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official GitHub release</a>; checksums, signature evidence, and an SBOM accompany new releases.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="download-details" aria-labelledby="details-title">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">what comes with it</p>
      <h2 id="details-title">A smaller browser surface. The browser essentials, built in.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="download-detail-list">
      <article>
        <h3>One floating island</h3>
        <p>Tabs, navigation and page controls share a compact Island in a slim top band. Its expanded panel opens over the page.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Built-in blocking</h3>
        <p>Blanc can block ads and known trackers without asking you to start with an extension.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Private tabs</h3>
        <p>Private activity stays out of Blanc history, session restore, and reopen-closed.</p>
      </article>
      <article><h3>A start page you can choose</h3><p>Four layouts include Billboard’s local frequent sites, and every footer opens standalone Mahjong with eight boards, Daily deals, and device-local records. <a href="/support#start-page">Explore the Start Page</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Room for a reference</h3><p><a href="/support#glance">Glance</a> puts another open tab beside your main page. <a href="/support#profiles">Local profiles and independent windows</a> keep browsing identities separate.</p></article>
      <article><h3>A way back after a close</h3><p><a href="/support#reopen-closed-tabs">Recently Closed</a> lets you reopen ordinary tabs or groups within a bounded, per-window undo history. Pages may reload.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Your bookmarks, brought along</h3><p>First-run setup helps with default-browser and privacy choices. In Favorites, import from a detected browser profile or an HTML bookmarks file. Imports happen on this device.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Optional Named Workspaces</h3><p><a href="/support#workspaces">Blanc Patron</a> adds saved sets of tabs and groups on this device. Ordinary tab groups remain free.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="download-footnote" aria-label="Download details">
    <p>Every download button points to the latest Blanc release on GitHub. If your download does not start, <a href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open the release page</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/privacy">Read how Blanc handles your data</a>, <a href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/blob/main/docs/release-verification.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">verify a release</a>, or email <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:support@blancbrowser.com">support@blancbrowser.com</a><!--/email_off--> if you need a hand.</p>
  </section>
</main>
<script>
  import { initHandheldDownload } from '../scripts/handheld-download.js';
  initHandheldDownload();
</script>
</BaseLayout>
